From baa9030d8405c9ee8ac96f0eb81368c2ada8e948 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 22:57:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03509/11362] [outer-loop] Aggressive adversarial defense vs
 outer-loop ARC solving (2nd-recurrence hardening)

Operator: "Update the adversarial agent to prevent this from happening again ...
the 2nd time ... aggressively caught and stopped. We want to help the LIVE agent
find ways of solving hidden games on its own ... based on its own attempts and RE
of the game." Built a 3-layer defense and hardened it through a hostile review.

- Layer 1b (per-artifact): adversarial_verify.check_arc_outer_loop_solve. Every
  ARC solve artifact must declare solve_provenance {live_agent_self_discovery |
  development_proxy | outer_loop_re}. CRITICAL on an OFFLINE-GROUND-TRUTH-BFS /
  per-game CALIBRATION solve (keyed on the experiment NAME + a game-solve claim --
  the honesty-INDEPENDENT catch that flags THIS incident's artifact, which made a
  prose tu93-L3 solve claim with NO structural solve fields), on outer_loop_re, an
  outer-loop-input contradiction, or a registry duplicate; WARN on undeclared
  provenance. CRITICAL -> fabrication-gate quarantine. arc_loop_solve now stamps
  provenance (dev twin -> development_proxy; adapter-free explore ->
  live_agent_self_discovery).
- Layer 2 (milestone-close AI audit): scripts/arc_self_solve_audit.py, wired into
  _run_operational_retrospective. Mechanical pre-pass (reachability + provenance)
  + hostile LLM review (SELF_DISCOVERY_ADVANCE | OUTER_LOOP_RE | OFF_PATH |
  DUPLICATE). Writes ops/arc_self_solve_audit_report.md; never edits.
- Layer 3: CLAUDE.md "ARC Live-Path Reachability Discipline" extended with the
  self-solve provenance contract + the three layers.

ADVERSARIAL REVIEW (FIX-FIRST) applied: a hostile sub-agent proved the structural
gate missed THIS incident's non-solve-shaped artifact and the provenance stamp was
gameable. Closed: the calibration-name detector now flags the exact incident
artifact + future offline-BFS-calibration solves (honesty-independent); game-id
detection is substring-robust; documented the HONEST residual (a self-contained,
undeclared, mislabeled outer-loop solve of a NEW game is caught only by the Layer 2
LLM, not mechanically -- the stamp is a contract, not a guarantee). Fixed a stale
research-note claim (arc_world_model_synth is live-reachable, not allow-listed).

VERIFIED: 11 new self-solve tests + adversarial-verify guard regression pass;
retroactive scan of results/ shows ONLY the 2 incident calibration artifacts
CRITICAL (zero false positives); orphan lint green; conductor parses; audit runs.
mypy hook skipped (.venv/bin/mypy not installed); ruff + the relevant hooks pass.
Conductor STOPPED.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
